{"ld": 847, "paper": "HP533", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, to Establish the Commission to Improve Tenant-Landlord Relationships and Increase the Use of Housing Vouchers (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-golek-cheryl", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bennett-richard", "h-debrito-flavia", "h-gere-traci", "h-malon-marc", "h-milliken-nina", "h-rana-ambureen", "h-roeder-amy", "s-talbot-ross-rachel", "h-yusuf-yusuf"], "committee_code": "JUD", "committee_name": "Judiciary", "summary": {"text": "This bill makes it a form of housing discrimination under the Maine Human Rights Act to refuse to rent or negotiate for the rental of a housing accommodation because of a person's source of money or other income. The bill also establishes, as a form of housing discrimination, assessing a person's ability to pay the entire rental amount when a portion of the rent is subsidized through federal, state or local housing assistance. In addition to any civil remedies available under the fair housing laws, a person aggrieved by a violation of these provisions is entitled to private remedies as an unfair trade practice as well as a monetary penalty of $1,000 or actual damages, whichever is greater. These provisions take effect January 1, 2026.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0533&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Died On Adjournment", "final_disposition": {"label": "Died On Adjournment", "date": "2026-04-29", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN084701.pdf", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 847)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0533&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-868)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0533&item=3&snum=132", "item": 3}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-